# Trivy vulnerability suppression file
# https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/
#
# All suppressed CVEs have been evaluated and fall into one of these categories:
#   1. Packages removed from the image at build time (no longer present — see
#      Dockerfile "MINIMAL RUNTIME STRIP": perl-base, apt, tar, openssl CLI)
#   2. Transitive dependencies not directly used by TFO Agent
#   3. Packages that cannot be purged (hard dependency chains / base system)
#   4. Patches pending from Debian trixie-security (not yet available upstream)

# =============================================================================
# perl-base: REMOVED from the image entirely (purged together with apt at the
# end of the runtime stage — see Dockerfile "MINIMAL RUNTIME STRIP"). The
# former perl-module CVEs (Archive::Tar, IO::Compress, HTTP::Tiny, Socket,
# Storable CVE-2026-57433, regex CVE-2026-13221) are obsolete: the interpreter
# is no longer present. No suppression entries needed.
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# tar: REMOVED from the image entirely (force-removed as the final dpkg
# operation — see Dockerfile "MINIMAL RUNTIME STRIP"). CVE-2026-5704 and the
# 2026-08 batch (CVE-2026-18477 TOCTOU, CVE-2026-18508 --one-top-level) are
# obsolete: the binary is no longer present. No suppression entries needed.
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# openssl / libssl3t64: CVE-2026-14456 — Denial of Service via unbounded
# memory growth in QUIC server (HIGH). Marked fix_deferred by Debian, no fixed
# version in trixie. libssl3t64 cannot be removed (Fluent Bit and libcurl4t64
# link it); the openssl CLI and openssl-provider-legacy ARE removed at build
# time. The QUIC *server* API is never used: OTLP runs gRPC/HTTP and Fluent
# Bit outputs over HTTP/TLS.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-14456

# =============================================================================
# libssh2-1t64: required by libcurl4t64 (SCP/SFTP support). No fixed version
# in trixie. CVE-2026-58050 (HIGH, heap overflow via integer overflow in
# publickey attribute allocation), CVE-2026-58051 (malformed SSH publickey
# response), CVE-2026-66032 (SFTP double-free), CVE-2026-66033 (AES-GCM
# integer underflow), CVE-2026-66034/66035 (SSH negotiation overflows) are
# all only reachable through SCP/SFTP transfers. The agent and Fluent Bit use
# HTTP/TLS outputs exclusively — no scp:/sftp: URL is ever requested.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-58050
CVE-2026-58051
CVE-2026-66032
CVE-2026-66033
CVE-2026-66034
CVE-2026-66035
CVE-2026-7598

# =============================================================================
# libsystemd0 / libudev1: CVE-2026-16742 (systemd-homed local privilege
# escalation) and CVE-2026-15059 (local users can terminate arbitrary
# processes). Both libraries stay: Fluent Bit links libsystemd.so.0 (sd_notify
# only) and util-linux links libudev. The vulnerable components (systemd-homed
# daemon, PID 1 shutdown paths) are not shipped and no systemd daemon runs in
# the container — the agent runs as non-root (UID 10001, nologin) under the
# container runtime's init. No fixed version in trixie.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-15059
CVE-2026-16742

# =============================================================================
# libp11-kit0: CVE-2026-18938 — integer overflow in RPC attribute-array
# length calculation that under-allocates "on 32 bit systems" only. TFO Agent
# publishes linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 images exclusively — the vulnerable
# 32-bit code path does not exist in shipped builds. Cannot be purged:
# libcurl4t64 -> librtmp1 -> libgnutls30t64 -> libp11-kit0 is a hard chain.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-18938

# =============================================================================
# linux-pam (libpam-modules, libpam-modules-bin, libpam-runtime, libpam0g):
# Cannot be purged — required by login/passwd/system authentication. TFO Agent
# runs as non-root user (UID 10001) with nologin shell — PAM is never invoked.
# Patch pending from Debian trixie-security.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-54411

# =============================================================================
# krb5: Integer underflow in berval2tl_data() leads to heap out-of-bounds read
# (GHSA alerts #222-225). CVE-2026-11850 affects libkrb5-3, libgssapi-krb5-2,
# libk5crypto3, libkrb5support0. krb5 is pulled in transitively by
# libsasl2-2 / libcurl4t64 for GSSAPI auth. TFO Agent does not initiate
# Kerberos authentication — Fluent Bit uses basic auth, libpq uses TLS.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-11850

# =============================================================================
# glibc (libc6 / libc-bin): cannot be purged (required by every binary).
# Patches pending from Debian trixie-security. The 2026-08 batch —
# CVE-2026-6368 (process abort via invalid memory in wordexp) and
# CVE-2026-6791 (stack exhaustion during tilde expansion) — requires
# wordexp()/shell tilde expansion on attacker-controlled strings; nothing in
# the agent calls wordexp, and no untrusted input reaches a shell.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-5435
CVE-2026-5450
CVE-2026-5928
CVE-2026-6238
CVE-2026-6368
CVE-2026-6791

# =============================================================================
# libcurl4t64 / curl: Connection reuse and credential leak CVEs.
# TFO Agent uses libcurl only for Fluent Bit output and health checks —
# no proxy authentication, no SMB, no Negotiate auth in production.
# CVE-2026-8458 (unauthorized connection reuse due to logical error,
# 2026-08 batch, no fix in trixie): the agent performs no concurrent
# authenticated requests over shared connections that could be cross-used.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-5773
CVE-2026-6276
CVE-2026-3805
CVE-2026-1965
CVE-2026-3783
CVE-2026-3784
CVE-2026-4873
CVE-2026-5545
CVE-2026-6253
CVE-2026-6429
CVE-2026-7168
CVE-2026-8458
# Fluent Bit 5.0.9 base (curl 8.14.1): no upstream fix available yet. Not
# reachable from the agent's usage — SFTP/SCP host verification (CVE-2026-12064),
# proxy auth disclosure (CVE-2026-8927/9079), mTLS reuse bypass (CVE-2026-8932),
# TLS config mismatch (CVE-2026-8286), curl_easy_pause UAF (CVE-2026-9080),
# and SSL session cache disclosure (CVE-2026-9545) all require code paths the
# agent does not exercise (HTTP/TLS output + health checks only).
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8927
CVE-2026-8932
CVE-2026-9079
CVE-2026-9080
CVE-2026-9545

# =============================================================================
# util-linux / bsdutils / mount / login / libblkid1 / libmount1 / libsmartcols1
# / libuuid1 / liblastlog2-2: Cannot be purged (core system utilities).
# Agent runs as non-root (UID 10001) — mount(8), chfn, chsh are not accessible.
# CVE-2026-27456: TOCTOU in mount with loop devices — agent runs as non-root.
# CVE-2026-3184: hostname canonicalization — agent does not use hostname auth.
# CVE-2025-14104: Heap buffer overread in setpwnam() — not reachable from agent.
# CVE-2022-0563: Partial disclosure in chfn/chsh — not installed in agent image.
# GHSA alerts #234-269: libblkid Integer Overflow (dos.c), mount(8) TOCTOU
# (hook_owner.c, Target Path Redirection), LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 nosuid/noexec
# bypass — all require local SUID mount(8) access which is not available to
# the non-root agent process.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-27456
CVE-2026-3184
CVE-2025-14104
CVE-2022-0563

# =============================================================================
# ncurses-base / ncurses-bin / libtinfo6: Cannot be purged (terminal library
# required by base system). CVE-2025-69720: buffer overflow — not exploitable
# in agent (no terminal interaction, non-root user).
# =============================================================================
CVE-2025-69720

# =============================================================================
# zlib1g: Transitive dependency. CVE-2026-27171: DoS via CRC32 — agent
# does not process untrusted compressed input.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-27171

# =============================================================================
# libbz2-1.0: Transitive dependency. CVE-2026-42250 — not used at runtime.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-42250

# =============================================================================
# liblzma5: Transitive dependency. CVE-2026-34743 — not used at runtime.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-34743

# =============================================================================
# libsqlite3-0: Transitive dependency (version 3.46.1-7+deb13u1). TFO Agent
# builds with CGO_ENABLED=0 and has no SQLite Go driver in go.mod — the agent
# never calls into libsqlite3. Purged from the image where possible; if dpkg
# prevents removal (another package depends on it), these CVEs are inert.
# CVE-2026-11822: memory corruption in SQLite before 3.53.2 (GHSA alert #227).
# CVE-2026-11824: heap-based buffer overflow in SQLite before 3.53.2 (GHSA #228).
# CVE-2026-50812 / CVE-2026-50813 (2026-08 batch): Session Extension changeset
# DoS / information disclosure — the agent never enables SQLite sessions.
# No fixed version available in Debian trixie at time of writing.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824
CVE-2026-50812
CVE-2026-50813

# =============================================================================
# Newly surfaced in the Fluent Bit 5.0.9 image scan (debian trixie 13.6).
# All are core OS packages that cannot be purged; the agent runs as non-root
# (UID 10001, nologin) and does not exercise the vulnerable code paths. No
# fixed version is available from Debian trixie-security at time of writing.
# =============================================================================
# perl-base: REMOVED from the image — the 2026-08 interpreter-core findings
# (CVE-2026-13221 silently incorrect regex, CVE-2026-57432 S_measure_struct
# integer overflow, CVE-2026-57433 Storable DoS) are obsolete: no Perl
# interpreter ships in the image. No suppression entries needed.
# util-linux / libblkid1 / bsdutils / libmount1 / libsmartcols1 / libuuid1:
# CVE-2026-53615 — heap use-after-free in libblkid nested partition probing.
# Core system utilities; the agent does not probe block devices or partitions.
CVE-2026-53615
# gzip: CVE-2026-41992 — global buffer overflow in the LZH decompressor. The
# agent does not decompress untrusted .lzh/.Z archives via gzip.
CVE-2026-41992
# libacl1: CVE-2026-54369 — symlink traversal privilege escalation via libacl
# functions. Requires local ACL operations on attacker-controlled paths; the
# agent runs non-root and performs no getfacl/setfacl on untrusted trees.
CVE-2026-54369

# =============================================================================
# MEDIUM findings in the 5.0.9 image (debian trixie 13.6). Same non-reachable
# OS-base categories as above — core packages that cannot be purged, agent runs
# non-root and does not exercise the vulnerable paths. No fix in trixie yet.
# =============================================================================
# curl / libcurl: .netrc password lookup, super-cookie injection, Digest
# header reuse, wrong-connection reuse. Agent uses libcurl only for Fluent Bit
# HTTP/TLS output + health checks — no .netrc, cookies, or Digest auth.
CVE-2026-10536
CVE-2026-11856
CVE-2026-8924
CVE-2026-8926
# bsdutils / util-linux: CVE-2026-13595 — libblkid partition probing. Agent
# does not probe block devices.
CVE-2026-13595
# libp11-kit0: CVE-2026-13757 — stack exhaustion via unbounded recursion in
# RPC attribute parsing. Agent does not use PKCS#11 modules.
CVE-2026-13757
# gzip: CVE-2026-41991 — gzexe insecure temp file. Agent does not run gzexe.
CVE-2026-41991
# libacl1 / libattr1: CVE-2026-54370 / CVE-2026-54371 — symlink traversal via
# getfacl/setfacl/getfattr/setfattr. Agent runs non-root; no ACL/xattr ops on
# untrusted paths.
CVE-2026-54370
CVE-2026-54371
# libnghttp2-14: CVE-2026-58055 — nghttpx Upgrade request forwarding. Agent
# does not run the nghttpx proxy.
CVE-2026-58055
